{"id":"mahabharata-7-117","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":117,"title":"सप्तदशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 117 · Bhurishravas against Satyaki","summary":{"en":"Bhurishravas, enraged at the sight of Satyaki, attacks him, and the two shower arrows on each other. When Satyaki's weapons are spent, Krishna tells Arjuna to save him, and Arjuna prepares to act.","kn":"ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ಭೂರಿಶ್ರವ ಅವನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಬಾಣ ಸುರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯ ಆಯುಧ ಮುಗಿದಾಗ ಅವನನ್ನು ರಕ್ಷಿಸಲು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಸಿದ್ಧನಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सात्यकि को देखकर क्रुद्ध भूरिश्रवा उस पर आक्रमण करता है और दोनों एक-दूसरे पर बाण बरसाते हैं। सात्यकि के शस्त्र चुकने पर कृष्ण अर्जुन से उसे बचाने को कहते हैं और अर्जुन तैयार होते हैं।","te":"సాత్యకిని చూసి కోపించిన భూరిశ్రవుడు అతనిపై దాడి చేస్తాడు; ఇద్దరూ ఒకరిపై ఒకరు బాణాలు కురిపిస్తారు. సాత్యకి ఆయుధాలు అయిపోగా అతన్ని రక్షించమని కృష్ణుడు అర్జునునికి చెబుతాడు; అర్జునుడు సిద్ధమవుతాడు.","ta":"சாத்யகியைக் கண்டு சினமுற்ற பூரிசிரவஸ் அவனைத் தாக்க, இருவரும் அம்பு மழை பொழிகின்றனர். சாத்யகியின் ஆயுதங்கள் தீர, அவனைக் காக்கும்படி கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனிடம் கூற, அர்ஜுனன் ஆயத்தமாகிறான்.","ml":"സാത്യകിയെ കണ്ട് കോപിച്ച ഭൂരിശ്രവസ്സ് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; ഇരുവരും പരസ്പരം അമ്പുമഴ ചൊരിയുന്നു. സാത്യകിയുടെ ആയുധങ്ങൾ തീർന്നപ്പോൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ രക്ഷിക്കാൻ കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനനോട് പറയുന്നു; അർജുനൻ പ്രവർത്തിക്കാൻ ഒരുങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.117; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तमापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य सात्वतं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nक्रोधाद्भूरिश्रवा राजन्सहसा समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Satvata, wild in battle, approaching, Bhurishravas, O king, suddenly ran at him in anger."}},{"n":2,"text":"तमब्रवीन्महाबाहुः कौरव्यः शिनिपुंगवम् ।\nअद्य प्राप्तोऽसि दिष्ट्या मे चक्षुर्विषयमित्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed Kaurava said to the bull of the Shinis, \"By good fortune you have come within my sight today.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"चिराभिलषितं काममद्य प्राप्स्यामि संयुगे ।\nन हि मे मोक्ष्यसे जीवन्यदि नोत्सृजसे रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today in battle I will fulfill the wish long cherished. You will not escape me with your life unless you give up the fight.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"अद्य त्वां समरे हत्वा नित्यं शूराभिमानिनम् ।\nनन्दयिष्यामि दाशार्ह कुरुराजं सुयोधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today, having slain you in battle, always proud of being a hero, I will delight King Suyodhana, descendant of Dasharha.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"अद्य मद्बाणनिर्दग्धं पतितं धरणीतले ।\nद्रक्ष्यतस्त्वां रणे वीरौ सहितौ केशवार्जुनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today the two heroes, Keshava and Arjuna together, will see you fallen on the ground, burned by my arrows.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"अद्य धर्मसुतो राजा श्रुत्वा त्वां निहतं मया ।\nसव्रीडो भविता सद्यो येनासीह प्रवेशितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today the king, the son of Dharma, hearing that you have been killed by me, will at once be ashamed, he by whom you were sent in here.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"अद्य मे विक्रमं पार्थो विज्ञास्यति धनंजयः ।\nत्वयि भूमौ विनिहते शयाने रुधिरोक्षिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today Partha Dhananjaya will know my prowess, when you lie killed on the ground, drenched in blood.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"चिराभिलषितो ह्यद्य त्वया सह समागमः ।\nपुरा देवासुरे युद्धे शक्रस्य बलिना यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today I have long wished to meet you, as the strong Bali met Shakra in the old war of gods and asuras.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"अद्य युद्धं महाघोरं तव दास्यामि सात्वत ।\nततो ज्ञास्यसि तत्त्वेन मद्वीर्यबलपौरुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today I will give you a very dreadful fight, Satvata; then you will know truly my courage, strength and manhood.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"अद्य संयमनीं याता मया त्वं निहतो रणे ।\nयथा रामानुजेनाजौ रावणिर्लक्ष्मणेन वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today, killed by me in battle, you will go to Yama's realm, as Ravana's son was killed by Lakshmana, Rama's younger brother.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"अद्य कृष्णश्च पार्थश्च धर्मराजश्च माधव ।\nहते त्वयि निरुत्साहा रणं त्यक्ष्यन्त्यसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today Krishna, Partha and the king of dharma, when you are killed, Madhava, will no doubt give up the battle, their spirits gone.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"अद्य तेऽपचितिं कृत्वा शितैर्माधव सायकैः ।\nतत्स्त्रियो नन्दयिष्यामि ये त्वया निहता रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today, having honored you with sharp arrows, Madhava, I will delight the wives of those you killed in battle.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"चक्षुर्विषयसंप्राप्तो न त्वं माधव मोक्ष्यसे ।\nसिंहस्य विषयं प्राप्तो यथा क्षुद्रमृगस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having come within my sight, you will not escape, Madhava, like a small deer that has come into a lion's range.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"युयुधानस्तु तं राजन्प्रत्युवाच हसन्निव ।\nकौरवेय न संत्रासो विद्यते मम संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yuyudhana, laughing as it were, answered him, \"Kaurava, I have no fear in battle.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"स मां निहन्यात्संग्रामे यो मां कुर्यान्निरायुधम् ।\nसमास्तु शाश्वतीर्हन्याद्यो मां हन्याद्धि संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He would kill me in the fight who would make me weaponless; he would kill me for endless years who kills me in the fight.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"किं मृषोक्तेन बहुना कर्मणा तु समाचर ।\nशारदस्येव मेघस्य गर्जितं निष्फलं हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What use is much false speech? Act. Your roar is as fruitless as the thunder of an autumn cloud.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"श्रुत्वैतद्गर्जितं वीर हास्यं हि मम जायते ।\nचिरकालेप्सितं लोके युद्धमद्यास्तु कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing this roar, hero, I laugh. Let the fight long wished for in the world be today, Kaurava.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"त्वरते मे मतिस्तात त्वयि युद्धाभिकाङ्क्षिणि ।\nनाहत्वा संनिवर्तिष्ये त्वामद्य पुरुषाधम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My mind is in haste, friend, with you wishing for battle. I will not turn back today without killing you, lowest of men.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"अन्योन्यं तौ तदा वाग्भिस्तक्षन्तौ नरपुंगवौ ।\nजिघांसू परमक्रुद्धावभिजघ्नतुराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two bulls among men, cutting at each other with words, wishing to kill, very angry, struck each other in the battle."}},{"n":20,"text":"समेतौ तौ नरव्याघ्रौ शुष्मिणौ स्पर्धिनौ रणे ।\nद्विरदाविव संक्रुद्धौ वाशितार्थे मदोत्कटौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two tigers among men, mighty and vying in the battle, met like two angry elephants, wild with rut, for a female."}},{"n":21,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः सात्यकिश्च ववर्षतुररिंदमौ ।\nशरवर्षाणि भीमानि मेघाविव परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas and Satyaki, tamers of foes, rained terrible showers of arrows on each other, like two clouds."}},{"n":22,"text":"सौमदत्तिस्तु शैनेयं प्रच्छाद्येषुभिराशुगैः ।\nजिघांसुर्भरतश्रेष्ठ विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Somadatta, wishing to kill, covered the Shini's grandson with swift arrows and struck him with sharp ones, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":23,"text":"दशभिः सात्यकिं विद्ध्वा सौमदत्तिरथापरान् ।\nमुमोच निशितान्बाणाञ्जिघांसुः शिनिपुंगवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having pierced Satyaki with ten arrows, Somadatta's son loosed others, sharp, wishing to kill the bull of the Shinis."}},{"n":24,"text":"तानस्य विशिखांस्तीक्ष्णानन्तरिक्षे विशां पते ।\nअप्राप्तानस्त्रमायाभिरग्रसत्सात्यकिः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, lord of the people, swallowed up with the tricks of his weapon those sharp arrows of his in the air before they arrived."}},{"n":25,"text":"तौ पृथक्शरवर्षाभ्यामवर्षेतां परस्परम् ।\nउत्तमाभिजनौ वीरौ कुरुवृष्णियशस्करौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two heroes, the fame-makers of the Kurus and Vrishnis, of the highest birth, rained showers of arrows on each other separately."}},{"n":26,"text":"तौ नखैरिव शार्दूलौ दन्तैरिव महाद्विपौ ।\nरथशक्तिभिरन्योन्यं विशिखैश्चाप्यकृन्तताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like two tigers with claws and two great elephants with tusks, they cut each other with chariot-javelins and arrows."}},{"n":27,"text":"निर्भिदन्तौ हि गात्राणि विक्षरन्तौ च शोणितम् ।\nव्यष्टम्भयेतामन्योन्यं प्राणद्यूताभिदेविनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tearing each other's limbs and pouring blood, they braced each other like two gamblers staking their lives."}},{"n":28,"text":"एवमुत्तमकर्माणौ कुरुवृष्णियशस्करौ ।\nपरस्परमयुध्येतां वारणाविव यूथपौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So those two of excellent deeds, glories of the Kurus and Vrishnis, fought each other like two leaders of herds of elephants."}},{"n":29,"text":"तावदीर्घेण कालेन ब्रह्मलोकपुरस्कृतौ ।\nजिगीषन्तौ परं स्थानमन्योन्यमभिजघ्नतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a long time those two, honored as if for Brahma's world, wishing to win the highest place, struck each other."}},{"n":30,"text":"सात्यकिः सौमदत्तिश्च शरवृष्ट्या परस्परम् ।\nहृष्टवद्धार्तराष्ट्राणां पश्यतामभ्यवर्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki and Somadatta's son rained arrows on each other, while the Dhritarashtra men looked on delighted."}},{"n":31,"text":"संप्रैक्षन्त जनास्तत्र युध्यमानौ युधां पती ।\nयूथपौ वाशिताहेतोः प्रयुद्धाविव कुञ्जरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The people there watched those two lords of fighters fighting, like two leaders of herds of elephants fighting over a female."}},{"n":32,"text":"अन्योन्यस्य हयान्हत्वा धनुषी विनिकृत्य च ।\nविरथावसियुद्धाय समेयातां महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed each other's horses and cut each other's bows, they, chariotless, came together for sword-fighting in the great battle."}},{"n":33,"text":"आर्षभे चर्मणी चित्रे प्रगृह्य विपुले शुभे ।\nविकोशौ चाप्यसी कृत्वा समरे तौ विचेरतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking broad, handsome shields of bull's hide, marvelously painted, and drawing their unsheathed swords, they ranged the battle."}},{"n":34,"text":"चरन्तौ विविधान्मार्गान्मण्डलानि च भागशः ।\nमुहुराजघ्नतुः क्रुद्धावन्योन्यमरिमर्दनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Moving in various paths and circles by turns, those two crushers of foes, angry, struck each other again and again."}},{"n":35,"text":"सखड्गौ चित्रवर्माणौ सनिष्काङ्गदभूषणौ ।\nरणे रणोत्कटौ राजन्नन्योन्यं पर्यकर्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With swords, with brightly colored armor, wearing gold ornaments and armlets, those two eager in battle, O king, dragged each other."}},{"n":36,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव राजेन्द्र परिकृष्य परस्परम् ।\nपश्यतां सर्वसैन्यानां वीरावाश्वसतां पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having dragged each other for a moment, O king of kings, those two heroes caught their breath again while all the armies watched."}},{"n":37,"text":"असिभ्यां चर्मणी शुभ्रे विपुले च शरावरे ।\nनिकृत्य पुरुषव्याघ्रौ बाहुयुद्धं प्रचक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having cut each other's shields, bright and broad, and the arrow-guards with their swords, those two tigers among men began wrestling with their arms."}},{"n":38,"text":"व्यूढोरस्कौ दीर्घभुजौ नियुद्धकुशलावुभौ ।\nबाहुभिः समसज्जेतामायसैः परिघैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Broad-chested, long-armed, both skilled in wrestling, they closed with their arms as with iron bars."}},{"n":39,"text":"तयोरासन्भुजाघाता निग्रहप्रग्रहौ तथा ।\nशिक्षाबलसमुद्भूताः सर्वयोधप्रहर्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Between them there were blows of the arms, holds and releases, born of the strength of training, delighting all warriors."}},{"n":40,"text":"तयोर्नृवरयो राजन्समरे युध्यमानयोः ।\nभीमोऽभवन्महाशब्दो वज्रपर्वतयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those two best of men fought in the battle, O king, a great sound arose, terrible, like that of the thunderbolt and a mountain."}},{"n":41,"text":"द्विपाविव विषाणाग्रैः शृङ्गैरिव महर्षभौ ।\nयुयुधाते महात्मानौ कुरुसात्वतपुंगवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like two elephants with the tips of tusks, like two great bulls with horns, those two great-souled bulls of the Kurus and Satvatas fought."}},{"n":42,"text":"क्षीणायुधे सात्वते युध्यमाने\nततोऽब्रवीदर्जुनं वासुदेवः ।\nपश्यस्वैनं विरथं युध्यमानं\nरणे केतुं सर्वधनुर्धराणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Satvata, his weapons spent, was fighting, Vasudeva then said to Arjuna, \"Look at him fighting chariotless, the banner of all archers in battle.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"प्रविष्टो भारतीं सेनां तव पाण्डव पृष्ठतः ।\nयोधितश्च महावीर्यैः सर्वैर्भारत भारतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He entered the Bharata army behind you, Pandava, and was fought by all those Bharatas of great valor.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"परिश्रान्तो युधां श्रेष्ठः संप्राप्तो भूरिदक्षिणम् ।\nयुद्धकाङ्क्षिणमायान्तं नैतत्सममिवार्जुन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Exhausted, the best of fighters, he has come against Bhuridakshina, who comes eager for the fight. This is not even, Arjuna.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"ततो भूरिश्रवाः क्रुद्धः सात्यकिं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nउद्यम्य न्यहनद्राजन्मत्तो मत्तमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhurishravas, angry, O king, raised Satyaki, wild in battle, and struck him down, as a rutting elephant does another."}},{"n":46,"text":"रथस्थयोर्द्वयोर्युद्धे क्रुद्धयोर्योधमुख्ययोः ।\nकेशवार्जुनयो राजन्समरे प्रेक्षमाणयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the two chief warriors, Keshava and Arjuna, angry, stood in their chariots watching in the battle, O king,"}},{"n":47,"text":"अथ कृष्णो महाबाहुरर्जुनं प्रत्यभाषत ।\nपश्य वृष्ण्यन्धकव्याघ्रं सौमदत्तिवशं गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"mighty-armed Krishna then said to Arjuna, \"Look at that tiger of the Vrishnis and Andhakas fallen into the power of Somadatta's son.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"परिश्रान्तं गतं भूमौ कृत्वा कर्म सुदुष्करम् ।\nतवान्तेवासिनं शूरं पालयार्जुन सात्यकिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Exhausted, fallen to the ground after doing a very hard deed, he is your pupil and a hero: protect Satyaki, Arjuna.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"न वशं यज्ञशीलस्य गच्छेदेष वरारिहन् ।\nत्वत्कृते पुरुषव्याघ्र तदाशु क्रियतां विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let this slayer of the best of enemies not come into the power of one devoted to sacrifice. For your sake, tiger among men, do that quickly, lord.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"अथाब्रवीद्धृष्टमना वासुदेवं धनंजयः ।\nपश्य वृष्णिप्रवीरेण क्रीडन्तं कुरुपुंगवम् ।\nमहाद्विपेनेव वने मत्तेन हरियूथपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dhananjaya, glad at heart, said to Vasudeva, \"Look at the bull of the Kurus playing with the Vrishni hero, like a lion with a rutting great elephant in a forest.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"हाहाकारो महानासीत्सैन्यानां भरतर्षभ ।\nयदुद्यम्य महाबाहुः सात्यकिं न्यहनद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry of dismay arose from the armies, best of Bharatas, when the mighty-armed one raised Satyaki and struck him on the ground."}},{"n":52,"text":"स सिंह इव मातङ्गं विकर्षन्भूरिदक्षिणः ।\nव्यरोचत कुरुश्रेष्ठः सात्वतप्रवरं युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dragging the best of the Satvatas like a lion dragging an elephant, Bhuridakshina, best of the Kurus, shone in the battle."}},{"n":53,"text":"अथ कोशाद्विनिष्कृष्य खड्गं भूरिश्रवा रणे ।\nमूर्धजेषु निजग्राह पदा चोरस्यताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhurishravas, drawing his sword from its sheath in the battle, seized him by the hair and struck his chest with his foot."}},{"n":54,"text":"तथा तु परिकृष्यन्तं दृष्ट्वा सात्वतमाहवे ।\nवासुदेवस्ततो राजन्भूयोऽर्जुनमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Satvata being dragged so in the battle, O king, Vasudeva again said to Arjuna,"}},{"n":55,"text":"पश्य वृष्ण्यन्धकव्याघ्रं सौमदत्तिवशं गतम् ।\nतव शिष्यं महाबाहो धनुष्यनवरं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Look at the tiger of the Vrishnis and Andhakas fallen into the power of Somadatta's son, your pupil, mighty-armed one, no less than you in archery.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"असत्यो विक्रमः पार्थ यत्र भूरिश्रवा रणे ।\nविशेषयति वार्ष्णेयं सात्यकिं सत्यविक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where Bhurishravas in the battle overpowers Satyaki, Vrishni's son of true valor, his valor is not false, Partha.\""}},{"n":57,"text":"एवमुक्तो महाबाहुर्वासुदेवेन पाण्डवः ।\nमनसा पूजयामास भूरिश्रवसमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so by Vasudeva, the mighty-armed Pandava honored Bhurishravas in his mind in the battle."}},{"n":58,"text":"विकर्षन्सात्वतश्रेष्ठं क्रीडमान इवाहवे ।\nसंहर्षयति मां भूयः कुरूणां कीर्तिवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dragging the best of the Satvatas as if playing in the fight, the increaser of the Kurus' fame gives me joy again,\""}},{"n":59,"text":"प्रवरं वृष्णिवीराणां यन्न हन्याद्धि सात्यकिम् ।\nमहाद्विपमिवारण्ये मृगेन्द्र इव कर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"in that he does not kill Satyaki, best of the Vrishni heroes, but drags him as a lion drags a great elephant in a forest.\""}},{"n":60,"text":"एवं तु मनसा राजन्पार्थः संपूज्य कौरवम् ।\nवासुदेवं महाबाहुरर्जुनः प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, O king, Partha, having honored the Kaurava in his mind, said to Vasudeva, the mighty-armed one,"}},{"n":61,"text":"सैन्धवासक्तदृष्टित्वान्नैनं पश्यामि माधव ।\nएष त्वसुकरं कर्म यादवार्थे करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With my eyes fixed on Saindhava, Madhava, I do not see him. But this hard deed I shall do for the Yadava's sake.\""}},{"n":62,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा वचनं कुर्वन्वासुदेवस्य पाण्डवः ।\nसखड्गं यज्ञशीलस्य पत्रिणा बाहुमच्छिनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, doing Vasudeva's word, the Pandava cut with an arrow the arm of that man devoted to sacrifice, with the sword in it."}}]}]}